{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "02734",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 1.3,
      "end_seconds": 4.62,
      "duration_seconds": 3.32,
      "text": "Okay, good afternoon, how are you today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 6.49,
      "end_seconds": 11.32,
      "duration_seconds": 4.83,
      "text": "Hello, doctor, I came in with them, if that's okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 13.11,
      "end_seconds": 19.49,
      "duration_seconds": 6.38,
      "text": "Of course, please stay. It's helpful to have you here. What do you need help with?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 21.05,
      "end_seconds": 26.01,
      "duration_seconds": 4.96,
      "text": "He's been having bright red blood on the paper, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 27.28,
      "end_seconds": 30.14,
      "duration_seconds": 2.86,
      "text": "What's the timeline, when did it begin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 31.58,
      "end_seconds": 42.88,
      "duration_seconds": 11.3,
      "text": "It's been about a week now. I'm hoping you can tell me something definite. I told my wife I'd come today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 43.82,
      "end_seconds": 50.27,
      "duration_seconds": 6.45,
      "text": "I was just going to say that the main thing is—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 50.37,
      "end_seconds": 57.47,
      "duration_seconds": 7.1,
      "text": "Sorry to cut in, doctor, quick question: shall I bring the trolley in now or later?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 58.65,
      "end_seconds": 60.9,
      "duration_seconds": 2.25,
      "text": "Later, thanks. Please go on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 62.66,
      "end_seconds": 72.76,
      "duration_seconds": 10.1,
      "text": "I mean, as for itching, I honestly can't say when that began. It might have been last month or the month before."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 73.37,
      "end_seconds": 76.21,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "Nothing like change in bowel habit?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 77.82,
      "end_seconds": 81.17,
      "duration_seconds": 3.35,
      "text": "No. No change in bowel habit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 81.89,
      "end_seconds": 87.83,
      "duration_seconds": 5.94,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any black stools, tummy pain or weight loss?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 89.86,
      "end_seconds": 106.35,
      "duration_seconds": 16.49,
      "text": "No, no black stools, no tummy pain, no weight loss. I did have a lump around the back passage at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 108.36,
      "end_seconds": 113.21,
      "duration_seconds": 4.85,
      "text": "Have you noticed any weakness, or anything odd with your balance?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 114.9,
      "end_seconds": 117.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.25,
      "text": "No weakness or anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 120.44,
      "end_seconds": 122.98,
      "duration_seconds": 2.54,
      "text": "So, anything surgical in your history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 123.97,
      "end_seconds": 129.44,
      "duration_seconds": 5.47,
      "text": "Ah, just a wisdom tooth extraction under sedation, five years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 131.12,
      "end_seconds": 133.74,
      "duration_seconds": 2.62,
      "text": "Do you have any long-term conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 135.76,
      "end_seconds": 161.71,
      "duration_seconds": 25.95,
      "text": "I have thin bones, for five years. I looked a few things up online, and that probably didn't help. I did try to ignore it for a while. Gout, for two years. I mean, I've had anxiety, yes. I'd rather know what's going on than keep guessing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 162.47,
      "end_seconds": 168.22,
      "duration_seconds": 5.75,
      "text": "Yes, thin bones and anxiety are known to us, good to have that clear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 179.96,
      "end_seconds": 183.56,
      "duration_seconds": 3.6,
      "text": "Do you take any prescribed or over-the-counter medicines?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 184.59,
      "end_seconds": 189.56,
      "duration_seconds": 4.97,
      "text": "Yeah, it's alendronate, once a week for my bones."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 190.91,
      "end_seconds": 193.22,
      "duration_seconds": 2.31,
      "text": "Do you know the dose?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 194.79,
      "end_seconds": 196.32,
      "duration_seconds": 1.53,
      "text": "It's 70 milligrams."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 198.4,
      "end_seconds": 200.85,
      "duration_seconds": 2.45,
      "text": "Right, and for how long?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 202.83,
      "end_seconds": 216.58,
      "duration_seconds": 13.75,
      "text": "For about a month. Actually, I'm on febuxostat, 80 milligrams, once a day. I'm on escitalopram, 10 milligrams, once a day for the anxiety."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 218.4,
      "end_seconds": 220.57,
      "duration_seconds": 2.17,
      "text": "Is there someone at home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 222.41,
      "end_seconds": 226.59,
      "duration_seconds": 4.18,
      "text": "My husband and I live above the shop."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 227.11,
      "end_seconds": 230.16,
      "duration_seconds": 3.05,
      "text": "What do you do during the day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 231.78,
      "end_seconds": 235.66,
      "duration_seconds": 3.88,
      "text": "I look after my grandchildren most days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 237.05,
      "end_seconds": 240.57,
      "duration_seconds": 3.52,
      "text": "Are there any allergies I should be aware of?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 241.77,
      "end_seconds": 243.37,
      "duration_seconds": 1.6,
      "text": "No known allergies."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 259.77,
      "end_seconds": 263.57,
      "duration_seconds": 3.8,
      "text": "Is there anything relevant on the family side?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 264.98,
      "end_seconds": 268.35,
      "duration_seconds": 3.37,
      "text": "My daughter has type 1 diabetes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 269.42,
      "end_seconds": 278.58,
      "duration_seconds": 9.16,
      "text": "Here are the numbers, doctor. Oxygen saturation is 97 percent, temperature 36.8, pulse is 75 beats a minute. Blood pressure 127 over 80."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 280.24,
      "end_seconds": 303.37,
      "duration_seconds": 23.13,
      "text": "Thanks. Listening to the whole story, my working impression is haemorrhoids. The reason I say that is that the way you describe it fits together. An anal fissure is also on my list. So, to recap quickly. You've had bright red blood on the paper for about a week, and no tummy pain or change in bowel habit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 304.15,
      "end_seconds": 306.31,
      "duration_seconds": 2.16,
      "text": "That's what happened, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 308.21,
      "end_seconds": 345.14,
      "duration_seconds": 36.93,
      "text": "I'm sending you for a blood count because of rectal bleeding. It's a routine test and it'll give us a much clearer picture. What I'm giving you is a haemorrhoid cream, 1 application, twice a day, one week. That's for haemorrhoids. What I'm giving you is lactulose, 15 ml, twice a day, four weeks. That's for constipation. Eat more fibre and drink water. One warning sign to remember: the symptoms get worse. In that case don't wait."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 346.78,
      "end_seconds": 352.65,
      "duration_seconds": 5.87,
      "text": "I'd like to see you again in four weeks. That's all from me. Any questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 354.37,
      "end_seconds": 356.48,
      "duration_seconds": 2.11,
      "text": "Thank you, doctor, goodbye."
    }
  ]
}